        "How the decision arrived: 'inbox' (the Hermiq approvals inbox) or 'reaction' (a 👍/👎 on the Talk message). Derived — written by the decision path, never by a user — so an audit reader can distinguish a one-click approval from a considered one. Deliberately not an enum, so a future decision surface can record itself without a schema change.": "How the decision arrived: 'inbox' (the Hermiq approvals inbox) or 'reaction' (a 👍/👎 on the Talk message). Derived — written by the decision path, never by a user — so an audit reader can distinguish a one-click approval from a considered one. Deliberately not an enum, so a future decision surface can record itself without a schema change.",
