        "The fleet MCP tool grant list, enforced at turn assembly. Entries: an exact id ({appId}.{toolName} or {app}.{schema}.{verb}) grants that tool verbatim; {app}.{schema}.* grants that schema's read verbs only (search/get); {app}.{schema}.*:write additionally grants its write verbs (create/update/delete). An EMPTY array grants NOTHING — no tools configured means no tools, with no override (see ToolGrantResolver). A schema wildcard NEVER grants write/destructive tools by default (default-deny) — name them explicitly, or add the :write modifier, to grant them. A NEW agent starts with the three capability meta-tools so it can find what it lacks and ask for it: searchTools (what it holds), listAvailableTools (what exists that it does not hold) and requestToolAccess (ask the owner). None of the three touches your data or grants anything by itself. ⚠️ That starting set is applied by AgentsController::create(), NOT by this `default` — OpenRegister does not materialise property defaults on create (verified: an agent POSTed without `tools` came back with no `tools` key at all), so a default declared here would be inert and would read as enforced.": "The fleet MCP tool grant list, enforced at turn assembly. Entries: an exact id ({appId}.{toolName} or {app}.{schema}.{verb}) grants that tool verbatim; {app}.{schema}.* grants that schema's read verbs only (search/get); {app}.{schema}.*:write additionally grants its write verbs (create/update/delete). An EMPTY array grants NOTHING — no tools configured means no tools, with no override (see ToolGrantResolver). A schema wildcard NEVER grants write/destructive tools by default (default-deny) — name them explicitly, or add the :write modifier, to grant them. A NEW agent starts with the three capability meta-tools so it can find what it lacks and ask for it: searchTools (what it holds), listAvailableTools (what exists that it does not hold) and requestToolAccess (ask the owner). None of the three touches your data or grants anything by itself. ⚠️ That starting set is applied by AgentsController::create(), NOT by this `default` — OpenRegister does not materialise property defaults on create (verified: an agent POSTed without `tools` came back with no `tools` key at all), so a default declared here would be inert and would read as enforced.",
