        "completed = every case executed (individual cases may still fail their own assertion); failed = an infrastructure-level error (e.g. no LLM provider configured) hit at least one case; blocked_killswitch/blocked_budget = the run never executed any case because the target organisation's kill-switch was engaged or its budget hard cap was reached; draft-comparison = a skill-self-improvement draft-vs-active pre-qualification comparison — deliberately NOT 'completed' so it can never become a regression-gate baseline and never writes levelEvidence.l5.": "completed = every case executed (individual cases may still fail their own assertion); failed = an infrastructure-level error (e.g. no LLM provider configured) hit at least one case; blocked_killswitch/blocked_budget = the run never executed any case because the target organisation's kill-switch was engaged or its budget hard cap was reached; draft-comparison = a skill-self-improvement draft-vs-active pre-qualification comparison — deliberately NOT 'completed' so it can never become a regression-gate baseline and never writes levelEvidence.l5.",
        "delivery-channels: base delay for exponential backoff between webhook delivery attempts (backoffBase * 2^(attempt-1)), retried synchronously within the same dispatch tick — a deliberately smaller-scale sibling of retryBackoffBaseSeconds (which retries the whole agent turn, in minutes, on a later tick), not a reuse of it.": "delivery-channels: base delay for exponential backoff between webhook delivery attempts (backoffBase * 2^(attempt-1)), retried synchronously within the same dispatch tick — a deliberately smaller-scale sibling of retryBackoffBaseSeconds (which retries the whole agent turn, in minutes, on a later tick), not a reuse of it.",
        "delivery-channels: total attempts (including the first) for one webhook delivery before it is recorded as failed. Mirrors retryMaxAttempts' shape at a different, seconds-scale timescale — see retryBackoffBaseSeconds' description for why it is not the same field.": "delivery-channels: total attempts (including the first) for one webhook delivery before it is recorded as failed. Mirrors retryMaxAttempts' shape at a different, seconds-scale timescale — see retryBackoffBaseSeconds' description for why it is not the same field.",
